Subject: [PATCH 6/6] docs(cdd): cdd-iteration.md as canonical home for
 self-iteration findings
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a first-class artifact under .cdd/ for cdd-self-improvement
findings surfaced by a cycle. The trigger mechanism (CDD.md §9.1)
and the disposition vocabulary (patch-landed / next-MCA / no-patch)
already exist; this patch adds the structured artifact where those
findings live, plus an aggregator and a cross-repo trace for
findings whose patch lands in a different repo than the source
cycle.

Three layers added under .cdd/:

  .cdd/unreleased/{N}/cdd-iteration.md
    per-cycle, conditionally required (only when triage produces
    >=1 finding tagged cdd-skill-gap / cdd-protocol-gap /
    cdd-tooling-gap / cdd-metric-gap), structured per-finding
    records with source / class / trigger / disposition /
    patch-or-issue link / affected cdd skill section

  .cdd/iterations/INDEX.md
    aggregator across all cycles that produced a cdd-iteration.md;
    one row per such cycle (Cycle / Issue / Date / Findings counts /
    Path); makes the cdd protocol's own learning rate measurable

  .cdd/iterations/cross-repo/{target-repo}/{slug}/
    bundle deliverables (patches, issue body, PR body, apply notes)
    plus LINEAGE.md mapping each deliverable to source cycle(s) and
    target repo PR; for findings whose patch lands cross-repo
    (e.g. cnos-tsc supercycle finding cnos cdd skill gaps);
    persists until target PR merges, then may be deleted

Files modified:

  cdd/CDD.md
    - §Tracking canonical filename table: add cdd-iteration.md row
    - §5.3a Artifact Location Matrix: add cdd-iteration, INDEX,
      cross-repo rows
    - §5.3b ownership matrix: add cdd-iteration.md and INDEX.md
      ownership rows tied to gamma closure gate

  cdd/post-release/SKILL.md
    - new Step 5.6b 'Author cdd-iteration.md (when applicable)'
      between existing 5.6a and 5.7
    - per-finding shape, aggregator update procedure, cross-repo
      trace procedure
    - pre-publish gate gains a checklist row enforcing the artifact
      when triage produces cdd-*-gap findings

  cdd/gamma/SKILL.md
    - §2.10 closure gate row 14 added: gamma cannot declare closure
      without the artifact when applicable

Motivation: the cnos-tsc supercycle (master usurobor/tsc#23,
5 cycles closed) produced 5 distinct cdd-skill-gap findings that
this very PR captures as patches 1-5. Reconstructing them required
reading 5 separate gamma-closeout.md files — exactly the friction
this artifact eliminates. The supercycle also exposed the cross-repo
case: findings surface in tsc, patches land in cnos. Without the
cross-repo trace structure, tsc's .cdd had no canonical home for
the bundle (the prior pr-bundles/ at repo root violated the 'all
artifacts under .cdd' principle).

This is recursive coherence — the patch defines the structure that
this very PR's cross-repo bundle uses.
